fix(test): hand the deploy harness the backup credential (#237)

db-init.sh now requires INNSEGL_BACKUP_PASSWORD, the same way it already
requires the appender's and the reader's. The Go harness that drives that
script does not go through compose, so it did not have it, and db-init exited 2
before provisioning anything — which failed every role test behind it and took
`test (race)` and `coverage floors` with them.

The harness carries the credential now, beside the other two. Nothing about the
tests' subject changed: they still measure the roles db-init produces, and the
backup role's own measurement rides along with them, because db-init gates on
verify-backup-role.sh and these tests run db-init.

